standards/effect-laws-v1.md:1:# Effect Laws v1
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:5:## Short Laws (authoritative)
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:25:14. HTTP boundaries must be expressed with Effect HTTP modules (`HttpClientRequest`, `HttpClientResponse`, `Headers`, `UrlParams`, `HttpMethod`, `HttpBody`).
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:26:15. JSDoc is required for exported APIs in `packages/*/src` and `packages/tooling/*/*/src`; examples must pass docgen.
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:29:18. Reusable `S.makeFilter`, `S.makeFilterGroup`, and reusable built-in check blocks must include `identifier`, `title`, and `description`; `message` stays user-facing.
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:30:19. Use `LiteralKit` for named internal literal domains, especially when `.Enum`, `.is`, `$match`, `.toTaggedUnion`, or annotation-bearing schema values are part of the design; use `S.Literals` for anonymous inline unions never referenced by name.
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:33:22. Reusable functions that directly return `Effect.gen(function*)` must use `Effect.fn` or `Effect.fnUntraced`; zero-arg one-off effect values may stay as `Effect.gen`.
standards/effect-laws-v1.md:34:23. Functions stay within the fallow complexity ceilings pinned in `.fallowrc.jsonc` `health` (the integers live in config, not prose). Every `fallow-ignore-*` suppression carries a `-- <reason>` (enforced by the `require-suppression-reason` rule); an honestly-complex function gets a `thresholdOverrides` entry with `reason` and a review date, never a bare suppression. Prefer real seams (match helpers, schema/data-table dispatch, named concept extraction) over threshold-appeasement fragmentation.
